From 1e4ab3ea2d1ecb8e1ec86c80dc35bd4cd29c3865 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: max rossi <113717219+maxr0ssi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 14:30:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 18/19] wined3d: Look up only active uniforms when linking a
 GLSL program.

A new program looks up the location of every uniform wined3d may declare: each vs_c[i] and
ps_c[i] up to the constant limit, the integer and boolean constants and the fixed function state,
about 700 names for an SM1-3 shader pair, nearly all of them absent. Each lookup is a call into
the driver, through the WoW64 thunks for a 32-bit application. List the program's active uniforms
first (a few dozen calls) and look up only names that are in the list, array elements within the
listed size. The first 16 programs are checked against the full lookup; a driver whose list
misses a uniform that has a location turns the shortcut off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
